tags: schedule, activity window

A condition of the node: the spans of the day in which it takes new work. Outside the
spans, the node is closed.

The value is the spans, separated by commas and sorted by their bytes. A span is
<start>-<end>, in minutes from 00:00 UTC, each from 0 to 1439, in base 10. A span with
start after end goes past midnight. Example: 480-1020,1320-120. The value is not
empty.

With no condition, the node is always open. The caller is bound: it accepts that the
node can close.

=== formal
class=condition
name=schedule
rule=the node takes new work only inside a span
value=the spans <start>-<end>, each a number of minutes (of 60 seconds) after 00:00:00 of the day in the time of the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:76016d6a59ad50c6aed0620ea7d772e9f3ec634a40cac7a94785b23768dae900, 0 to 1439, base 10, sorted, separated by commas; a start after its end goes past 00:00:00; not empty
